cell><cell>0.8817</cell><cell>0.7422</cell><cell>0.4868</cell><cell>0.6912</cell><cell>0.6053</cell><cell>0.7908</cell><cell>0.6463</cell></row><row><cell>Improv.</cell><cell cols=\"10\">+19.75% +8.22% +11.96% +7.25% +11.24% +15.77% +7.10% +9.72% +3.40% +7.59%</cell></row></table></figure>\n<figure xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" type=\"table\" xml:id=\"tab_3\"><head>Table 4 :</head><label>4</label><figDesc>Comprehensive ablation study on books.</figDesc><table><row><cell>Model Config.</cell><cell cols=\"2\">H@1 H@3 N@3 H@5 N@5 Drop</cell></row><row><cell>MemRec (Full)</cell><cell>0.527 0.713 0.634 0.803 0.670</cell><cell>-</cell></row><row><cell>w/o Collab. Write</cell><cell cols=\"2\">0.505 0.702 0.619 0.814 0.665 4.2%</cell></row><row><cell cols=\"3\">w/o LLM Curation 0.498 0.685 0.606 0.788 0.648 5.5%</cell></row><row><cell>w/o Collab. Read</cell><cell cols=\"2\">0.475 0.650 0.575 0.769 0.624 9.9%</cell></row></table></figure>\n<figure xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" type=\"table\" xml:id=\"tab_4\"><head>Table 5 :</head><label>5</label><figDesc>Comprehensive architectural analysis across different model configurations. Latency: average online time measured in our experimental setup (sequential execution). Tokens/U (On / Total): average tokens consumed per user during online inference versus the complete session (including asynchronous offline memory maintenance). Cost: qualitative estimate of online serving efficiency.The offline memory maintenance incurs zero API cost due to local hosting, leaving only the minimal online LLMRec cost. ‡ Local latency is hardware-dependent (measured sequentially on single NVIDIA A5000 GPU) and not directly comparable to highly optimized cloud APIs.</figDesc><table><row><cell></cell><cell cols=\"2\">Model Selection</cell><cell>Performance</cell><cell></cell><cell>Efficiency Metrics</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>Configuration</cell><cell>LLM Rec</cell><cell>LM Mem</cell><cell cols=\"5\">H@1 N@5 Latency Tokens/U (On / Total) Cost (Online) Key Takeaway</cell></row><row><cell>Vanilla LLM</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell>-</cell><cell>0.330 0.524</cell><cell>∼5.1s</cell><cell>∼1.2k / ∼1.2k</cell><cell>Lowest</cell><cell>No memory, fast but poor precision</cell></row><row><cell cols=\"5\">Single-User Mem 4o-mini 4o-mini (Iso.) 0.475 0.631 ∼10.0s</cell><cell>∼1.4k / ∼5.5k</cell><cell>Low</cell><cell>Memory overhead without collaboration</cell></row><row><cell>Standard</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell cols=\"2\">0.524 0.663 ∼16.5s</cell><cell>∼1.5k / ∼6.8k</cell><cell>Low</cell><cell>Collaborative gains over single-user</cell></row><row><cell>Vector</cell><cell>Vector</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell>0.209 0.387</cell><cell>∼5.3s</cell><cell>-/ ∼6.3k</cell><cell>Lowest</cell><cell>Ultra-fast, pluggable reranker</cell></row><row><cell>Local-Qwen</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell>Qwen-2.5-7B</cell><cell cols=\"2\">0.470 0.627 ∼34.0s  ‡</cell><cell>∼1.6k / ∼7.0k</cell><cell>Low ⋆</cell><cell>Best on-premise performance</cell></row><row><cell>Local-Llama</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell>Llama-3-8B</cell><cell cols=\"2\">0.360 0.550 ∼34.4s  ‡</cell><cell>∼1.4k / ∼6.2k</cell><cell>Low ⋆</cell><cell>Alternative local option</cell></row><row><cell>Ceiling</cell><cell>gpt-4o</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell cols=\"2\">0.580 0.722 ∼10.4s</cell><cell>∼1.5k / ∼6.9k</cell><cell>High</cell><cell>Peak performance, high serving cost</cell></row><row><cell>Cloud-OSS</cell><cell>4o-mini</cell><cell>OSS-120B</cell><cell cols=\"2\">0.561 0.699 ∼11.8s</cell><cell>∼1.8k / ∼10.0k</cell><cell>Low</cell><cell>Near-ceiling results w/ moderate cost</cell></row></table><note><p>⋆</p></note></figure>\n<figure xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" type=\"table\" xml:id=\"tab_5\"><head>Table 6 :</head><label>6</label><figDesc>Main results for Books and Goodreads (N=20). Notation follows Table2; all improvements are significant (p &lt; 0.05).</figDesc><table><row><cell></cell><cell></cel